From 946e7887a374868de4d562032f82ba81697c3c4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Heidelberg <david@ixit.cz>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 01:41:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 072/212] media: i2c: Add Samsung S5K2X7SP camera sensor driver

Add a minimal V4L2 subdevice driver for the Samsung S5K2X7SP raw image
sensor. The sensor is a 2x7-class CCS-compatible Samsung sensor using a
0x2a/0x2e burst register access pattern; it is brought up using the
register sequence extracted from the vendor camera XML for the SHIFT 6MQ
(axolotl) phone.

The driver supports a single 2832x2128 GRBG 10-bit 4-lane mode at 30 fps
on a 1150 MHz CSI link, with analogue gain, exposure, h/v flip and test
pattern controls. It is based on the existing s5k3m5 driver and uses the
V4L2 CCI helpers.

Signed-off-by: David Heidelberg <david@ixit.cz>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig         |   10 +
 drivers/media/i2c/Makefile        |    1 +
 drivers/media/i2c/s5k2x7sp.c      |  782 ++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/media/i2c/s5k2x7sp_regs.h | 1150 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 1943 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/media/i2c/s5k2x7sp.c
